From e34552859ee08609ac215a7f2220640127fc962d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Bright <William.Bright@imd-tec.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 15:01:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] media: i2c: ar1335: Convert to V4L2 CCI and fix streaming
 failures

Replace raw i2c_transfer() register access with the V4L2 CCI regmap
API. The previous bulk writes via ar1335_write_regs() sent up to 18
bytes in a single I2C message, exceeding the Qualcomm CCI adapter's
max_write_len of 11 bytes. The I2C quirks check rejected these with
-EOPNOTSUPP (-95), breaking streaming on CCI-attached sensors.

The CCI API writes one register per I2C transaction via regmap,
staying within adapter limits while still allowing bulk register
sequences through cci_multi_reg_write().

Additional fixes:
- Fix VCO calculation: use AR1335_PIXEL_CLOCK_RATE * vt_pix_div
  directly instead of incorrectly applying a per-lane divisor, which
  halved the pixel clock and reduced frame rate from 15 to ~8 fps
- Fix PLL register ordering: ar1335_calc_pll() was called after the
  register array was initialized, writing stale PLL values
- Restore blanking defaults to match the known-good XML configuration
  (hblank=464, vblank=30)
- Increase post-reset delay from 1-2ms to 20-25ms to allow the
  sensor to complete internal initialization (~300k EXTCLK cycles)
  before I2C access, fixing -ENXIO on runtime resume

Signed-off-by: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Needs checking with the
v4l2-compliance tool]
